      },
      {
        "purpose": "modern_jp_reading",
        "value": "来次権──"
      },
      {
        "purpose": "english_translation",
        "value": "Acting senior councillor, surname 來次 (read Kisugi; the reading is tentative). Three glyphs print, confirmed at 3x — 來 y2018-2080, 次 y2149-2207, 權 y2273-2334 — and a printed vertical rule then runs from y2354 to y2588, filling the cell to its foot. What the rule stands for cannot be settled from this leaf. The two 大參事 entries in the same registers print surname plus office title in full (土井大參事, 小杉大參事), which would make the rule a repetition mark for the rest of the title 大參事; alternatively it marks a given name the domain did not report. The rule in every case begins about 20 px below the last printed glyph and runs to the bottom of the cell rather than occupying a fixed number of glyph slots, and in the two-glyph entries the surname is set at a wider pitch (about 170 px against 127) to fill the space above it."
      },
      {
        "purpose": "identifying",
        "value": "古河藩權大參事來次權"
      }
